"""ultrackbench.py -- the REAL Ultrack pipeline (foreground/contour UNet ->
area hierarchy of segmentation hypotheses -> temporal ILP) on bench movies,
scored by the official metric and measured for node placement.

WHY (2026-09-13). The competition GT is Ultrack's segmentation of these
images (paper, sparse-labelling experiment). ultrackprobe showed that
Ultrack's own UNet, segmented at ONE watershed level, places the swap-site
cells no better than our maps (2.5-2.6 um vs 2.69) and sees two blobs around
the one annotated centroid at two thirds of swap sites; a GT made from that
segmentation can sit between two blobs only if the hierarchy + ILP chose the
merged hypothesis. Only the full pipeline can reproduce that choice. This
kernel runs it with the paper's sparse_zebrafish config and asks two things:
(1) where Ultrack's selected nodes land relative to the annotated centroids
(all annotated nodes, and the swap-site ones), and (2) what the official
metric gives Ultrack's own tracks on these movies against our shipped
pipeline's per-movie rows.

WHAT IT DOES. pip installs ultrack (internet ON; solver CBC via `mip`,
gurobipy unlicensed). For each movie in MOVIES, all frames: the UNet
(unet-daxi, percentile 1-99.9 input normalisation; the probe's best row)
gives foreground = channel 0, contours = channel 1. Ultrack config from
ultrack_supplementary/configuration/sparse_zebrafish/config.toml:
segmentation threshold 0.4, min_area 300, max_area 25000, min_frontier 0,
area hierarchy; linking max_distance 10, max_neighbors 5, distance_weight 0,
z_score 5; tracking appear/disappear/division -0.1, power 4, bias 0, window
25, overlap 5, gap 0.001. `Tracker.track(foreground, contours, scale)`.
Nodes and parent links come from `to_pandas`; a geff is written with the
bench's saver and scored with the official scorer (score_one). Placement:
for every annotated GT node, distance to the nearest Ultrack node in that
frame; recall at 5 / 7 um; the same at the swap-site GT children (hplace's
table). Ultrack's nodes are saved per movie (`ultrack_nodes_<name>.npz`:
id, parent_id, t, z, y, x) for reuse as a detection source.
Reference rows (dupsup REF F4HP, our shipped pipeline ungated):
  6bba_05b6850b adj_J 0.9976 edge_J 0.9941 tp/fp/fn 843/3/2 nodes 6,136
  6bba_05db0fb1 adj_J 0.8755 edge_J 0.8729 1106/84/77 nodes 67,745
  6bba_062c8d37 adj_J 0.9830 edge_J 0.9756 881/5/17  nodes 5,572
Attach: faustine649/cell-tracking, pilkwang support pack, the weights
dataset, the competition. GPU T4, internet on. Budget-guarded.
"""
